   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID-Africa Small Grants</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The purpose of this project is to identify where the critical sites for biodiversity conservation occur in the Albertine Rift by surveying amphibians, reptiles, small mammals, and plants and using the software Marxan to weigh the costs and benefits to conservation and development of alternative land-use decisions. It will: 1)finalize models of species distributions from existing data and identify sites of.potential importance to survey, 2) undertake field surveys of key identified sites, and 3) use Marxan to identify critical sites for biodiversity conservation in the Albertine Rift..and also where potential for trade-offs or offsets exist for development projects such.as mining&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
